Subject: [PATCH] fritchii2-grhand: a guest read of cached memory whose cache mutexes stay taken is answered with a

fritchii2-grhand: a guest read of cached memory whose cache mutexes stay taken is answered with a
flush request served by the back, instead of waiting for the mutexes.
Switch EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GRHAND=1, off by default.

Upstream: Frizti/Fritchii e423d1bd17 (EXP60=1; "live, off by default", never made a default, no
fps figure). Credit Frizti. Their reason: the split's back holds texture_cache.mutex and
buffer_cache.mutex through bursts of draws and takes them again right after each release, so a
guest read waiting for them lost to it draw after draw (guest threads asleep 5-6 ms in the frames
of the close-camera dips).

What it does (RasterizerVulkan::GetFlushArea): try the mutexes the read needs (texture unless
EDEN_PE_IMAGE_PAGES says no image ever held the pages, and buffer) up to 256 times with a yield in
between. All taken: the same answers as the normal path, under them. Not: return the read's pages
as a non-preemptive area; GPU::OnCPURead then queues InvalidateGPUCache + FlushRegion(pages) as a
sync request and waits; the back serves it after its current draw (PrepareDraw's SCOPE_EXIT
TickWork, as in Fritchii), and a flush of pages with nothing GPU-written does nothing.

Deviations: (1) an attempt that does not get every mutex releases what it got before yielding
(std::try_lock); Fritchii keeps the first while it retries the second, which holds the back up.
(2) Only while buffer_cache.FlushesOnCpuRead() (Switch 2 native tiling: true): with async buffer
downloads the request's FlushRegion would download buffer data this path never downloads on a
read, so the normal path runs (counted as "not handed"). (3) Our normal path asks the texture cache
first and the buffer cache only with FlushesOnCpuRead, both kept. (4) Counters every 5 s:
"EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GRHAND: guest reads of cached memory (N ms): L locked, H handed to the back as
flush requests, A not handed (async buffer downloads)".

Review fix (9 Nov): the handed answer skipped the caches' GetFlushArea, which also forgets the
pages' read trap (BufferCache::read_trapped_ranges) and marks GPU-written data for downloads at
fences (Preflushable, the images' PreemtiveDownload/forced_flushed). The core then kept the handed
pages as its read area, and the next GPU write there was deduplicated (ArmReadTraps finds the range
still armed) and did not move the read trap generation: the core could read older bytes until some
other arm moved it. The handed path now queues the same texture-then-buffer GetFlushArea calls for
the back (GPU::RunOnGpuThread) ahead of the flush request OnCPURead queues next. Sync requests run in
order and OnCPURead waits for the later one, so the side effects land before the guest reads.

Honest value for the PS5: low, possibly negative. Reads only get here for pages with a GPU-written
mark (HandleRasterizerDownload reads the rest directly) that miss the core's area. A handed read
still waits for the back's current draw (a pipeline build inside the draw is waited out in full
either way, so GrowingBlackBeans' "guest cores in HandleRasterizerDownload while the back builds a
pipeline" is not fixed by this), may re-download an image already downloaded at a fence
(forced_flushed, which the locked path would answer preemptively), remembers only the read's pages
instead of the image's range (more later misses), and spins up to 256 yields on a guest core, which
is our bottleneck. It only helps if the lock convoy is real here; the counters show whether reads
are handed at all. Gate (review): test only if EDEN_DEV_GUEST cpu_read_ns and cache_lock_blocked
in existing control logs show guest cores waiting on these locks for a real share of their time.

Files: src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp (compiled from the generated copy, made by
tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py; same anchor skips before and after). Unset: identical behaviour (one
static bool test per GetFlushArea).

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <fstream>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <string_view>
+#include <thread>
 #include <vector>
 #include <bit>
 #include <optional>
@@ -2238,8 +2239,111 @@ void RasterizerVulkan::FlushQueryResults(DAddr addr, u64 size) {
     fence_manager.SignalAndWait();
 }
 
+namespace {
+/// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GRHAND: guest reads of cached memory answered under the caches' mutexes, and
+/// those handed to the back as flush requests, logged every 5 s.
+struct GuestReadHandCounts {
+    std::atomic<u64> locked{};
+    std::atomic<u64> handed{};
+    std::atomic<u64> async_buffers{}; ///< not handed: the buffer cache flushes no CPU read
+    std::atomic<s64> last_log_ms{};
+};
+GuestReadHandCounts g_guest_read_hand;
+
+void CountGuestRead(std::atomic<u64>& counter) {
+    if (((counter.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1) & 255) != 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    auto& c = g_guest_read_hand;
+    const s64 now = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(
+                        std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch())
+                        .count();
+    s64 last = c.last_log_ms.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    if (now - last < 5000 ||
+        !c.last_log_ms.compare_exchange_strong(last, now, std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+             "EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GRHAND: guest reads of cached memory ({} ms): {} locked, {} handed "
+             "to the back as flush requests, {} not handed (async buffer downloads)",
+             last == 0 ? 0 : now - last, c.locked.exchange(0, std::memory_order_relaxed),
+             c.handed.exchange(0, std::memory_order_relaxed),
+             c.async_buffers.exchange(0, std::memory_order_relaxed));
+}
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 VideoCore::RasterizerDownloadArea RasterizerVulkan::GetFlushArea(DAddr addr, u64 size) {
     static const bool pages = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_PE_IMAGE_PAGES");
+    // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GRHAND=1 (Frizti/Fritchii e423d1bd17, there EDEN_NX2_EXP60=1; live there,
+    // off by default, no fps figure): the split's back holds both cache mutexes through bursts of
+    // draws and takes them again right after each release, so a guest read waiting for them can
+    // lose to it draw after draw (Fritchii saw guest threads asleep 5-6 ms there). Try a little;
+    // if a mutex stays taken, answer with a flush request for the read's pages instead: OnCPURead
+    // queues it and the back serves it after its current draw (PrepareDraw's TickWork), and a
+    // flush of pages with nothing GPU-written does nothing. Only while the buffer cache flushes
+    // on CPU reads (FlushesOnCpuRead): otherwise the request's FlushRegion would download buffer
+    // data this path never downloads on a read, and the path below runs as without the switch.
+    static const bool hand = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GRHAND");
+    if (hand && !buffer_cache.FlushesOnCpuRead()) [[unlikely]] {
+        CountGuestRead(g_guest_read_hand.async_buffers);
+    } else if (hand) [[unlikely]] {
+        const bool ask_texture = !pages || !Eden::ImagePages::NeverHeld(addr, size);
+        std::unique_lock texture_lock{texture_cache.mutex, std::defer_lock};
+        std::unique_lock buffer_lock{buffer_cache.mutex, std::defer_lock};
+        // Unlike Fritchii, which keeps a mutex it got while it retries the other, an attempt that
+        // does not get every mutex it needs releases them before it yields (std::try_lock), so
+        // the back is not held up by the guest's retries.
+        constexpr int Tries = 256;
+        bool held = false;
+        for (int attempt = 0; attempt < Tries && !held; ++attempt) {
+            held = ask_texture ? std::try_lock(texture_lock, buffer_lock) == -1
+                               : buffer_lock.try_lock();
+            if (!held) {
+                std::this_thread::yield();
+            }
+        }
+        if (!held) {
+            CountGuestRead(g_guest_read_hand.handed);
+            // The core keeps the area OnCPURead returns until the read trap generation moves.
+            // The caches' GetFlushArea is what forgets the pages' read trap (the buffer cache's
+            // read_trapped_ranges, so that the next GPU write there moves the generation again)
+            // and marks GPU-written data for downloads at fences (Preflushable, the images'
+            // PreemtiveDownload and forced_flushed). Skipped, the area would outlive the next GPU
+            // write to these pages and the core would read their older bytes. So the back runs
+            // the same calls as the path below, before the flush request OnCPURead queues next
+            // (sync requests run in order, and OnCPURead waits for the later one).
+            static_cast<void>(gpu.RunOnGpuThread([this, addr, size, ask_texture] {
+                if (ask_texture) {
+                    std::scoped_lock lock{texture_cache.mutex};
+                    if (texture_cache.GetFlushArea(addr, size)) {
+                        return;
+                    }
+                }
+                std::scoped_lock lock{buffer_cache.mutex};
+                static_cast<void>(buffer_cache.GetFlushArea(addr, size));
+            }));
+            return VideoCore::RasterizerDownloadArea{
+                .start_address = Common::AlignDown(addr, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE),
+                .end_address = Common::AlignUp(addr + size, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE),
+                .preemtive = false,
+            };
+        }
+        // Held: the answers of the path below, under the same mutexes.
+        CountGuestRead(g_guest_read_hand.locked);
+        if (ask_texture) {
+            if (auto area = texture_cache.GetFlushArea(addr, size)) {
+                return *area;
+            }
+        }
+        if (auto area = buffer_cache.GetFlushArea(addr, size)) {
+            return *area;
+        }
+        return VideoCore::RasterizerDownloadArea{
+            .start_address = Common::AlignDown(addr, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE),
+            .end_address = Common::AlignUp(addr + size, Core::DEVICE_PAGESIZE),
+            .preemtive = true,
+        };
+    }
     if (!pages || !Eden::ImagePages::NeverHeld(addr, size)) {
         static const bool skip = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_PE_CPU_READ_SKIP");
         std::unique_lock lock{texture_cache.mutex, std::defer_lock};
